{{Quote|For the first time in my life, I'm proud to wear this [[Wolverine Suit|suit]]. It means I'm an [[X-Men/Mutant Genocide|X-Man]]. I am the X-Man.|Wolverine to [[Deadpool]]|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
'''James Howlett''', more commonly referred to as '''Logan''', is a formidable [[Mutants|mutant]] with retractable claws and regenerative abilities operating under the alias '''Wolverine''', who failed both his teammates, the [[X-Men/Mutant Genocide|X-Men]], and his world, sending him into a depressive spiral. He was taken from his universe by [[Deadpool]] in the latter's attempt to replace his own reality's [[Wolverine/Anchor Being Wolverine|Wolverine]], though the two were banished to the [[Void]] by [[Mr. Paradox]]'s rogue faction of [[Time Variance Authority]] agents. Wolverine and Deadpool formed an initially very uneasy alliance to try and escape the Void, which they did with the aid of the [[Resistance]]. Now together as friends, the pair was able to stop Paradox's plan to destroy Deadpool's timeline and eliminate [[Cassandra Nova]] to save the entire [[Multiverse]], eventually allowing Logan to come to better terms with his past mistakes and live peacefully in Wade Wilson's universe.

==Biography==
===Early Life===
====Death of the X-Men====
{{Quote|[[Cyclops|Scott]] used to beg me to wear [[Wolverine Suit|it]]. So did [[Jean Grey|Jean]], [[Storm]], [[Beast/Mutant Genocide|Beast]]... All of [[X-Men/Mutant Genocide|them]]. They wanted me to be part of the team, but I wouldn't. Told them they all looked fuckin' ridiculous. I mean, I couldn't have 'em thinking I wanted to be there. And then one day while I was off on my own, the [[humans]] came. They went [[Mutants|mutant]] hunting."<br>"I can guess the rest."<br>"No, no, let me say it, I... I need to say it. By the time I stumbled home, shit-faced from the bar, it was too late. They were dead, every... This suit's all I've go to remind me of... who they were. What I did.|Logan and [[X-23|Laura]]|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
James Howlett was a [[Canada|Canadian]]-born [[Mutants|mutant]] that developed a regenerative healing factor and retractable [[adamantium]] claws. Eventually dubbing himself Logan, he often allied with the [[X-Men/Mutant Genocide|X-Men]], [[Professor X/Mutant Genocide|Charles Xavier]]'s team of mutants, and was offered a [[Wolverine Suit|suit]] by his teammates, though he rejected it in an effort to have them not think he wanted to be part of the team.

One day when he was off on his own, [[humans]], driven by fear and hatred towards [[mutants]], orchestrated a surprise attack on the [[X-Mansion]]. This led to the deaths of several [[X-Men/Mutant Genocide|X-Men]] members, including powerful mutants like [[Storm]], [[Beast/Mutant Genocide|Beast]], [[Cyclops]] and [[Jean Grey]]. Due to Logan's absence during the attack on the X-Men, he took the blame for their deaths upon himself and went on a rampage. His guilt and self-loath over not being there to protect his team. He was shunned by society and grew into a state of depression.{{Ref|DW}}

===[[Preservation of Earth-10005]]===
====Taken from His World====
[[File:Deadpool and Logan at a bar.jpg|{{AltFloat}}|Logan confronts [[Deadpool]]]]
{{Quote|Why would I go with you?"<br>"...Because, unfortunately, I need you. And even more unfortunately, my [[Anchor Being Wolverine|entire world]] needs you.|Logan and [[Deadpool]]|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
By a bar's counter, Logan was given another drink by a bartender who eagerly wanted him gone. Logan was approached by [[Deadpool]], also known as Wade Wilson, a person who claimed to know him and to need him for his [[Anchor Being Wolverine|world]]. Questioned by the bartender if they are going to fuck or fight, Logan didn't react to the insult, much to Deadpool's surprise. Deadpool, remarking that any other Wolverine would've hurt him by now and that he had little time, raised Logan up from his seat, Logan responding by popping his claws. His claws had grown miniscule, as Deadpool sarcastically noted before putting a gun to Logan's head. Logan simply laughed, drinking a whole bottle of beer while holding the gun for Deadpool to watch before collapsing to the floor.
[[File:Deadpool and Wolverine at the TVA.jpg|{{AltFloat}}|Wolverine rises behind [[Deadpool]]]]
Logan was taken into the [[Time Variance Authority Office]] through a [[Timedoor]] only dressed in his [[Wolverine Suit|suit]], falling on the floor yet hearing Deadpool and [[Time Variance Authority]] agent [[Mr. Paradox]]'s conversation about the impossibility of replacing what is known as an "Anchor Being," which was Deadpool's own Wolverine and Deadpool's actions do to so. Logan eventually rose up and was welcomed into the [[Marvel Cinematic Universe]] by Deadpool, albeit at a "low point." Deadpool went on to threaten Paradox by alerting his bosses, only to find out that they don't know. Logan was confused to see Deadpool pruned by a [[Time Stick]], which he was as well in his attempt to harm Paradox.{{Ref|DW}}

====Fight in the Void====
[[File:Deadpool & Wolverine Trailer (34).png|thumb|{{AltFloat}}|Wolverine tells [[Deadpool]] he doesn't care about his [[Anchor Being Wolverine|world]]]]
{{Quote|Let's see you grow your fucking head back!"<br>"Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait! I can fix it! I can fix it."<br>"Fix what?"<br>"Whatever it is you did. Whatever made you so bad. Those... those pricks at the [[TVA]], you heard them. They have the power to end my [[Anchor Being Wolverine|universe]]. But, also, they have the power to change [[Mutant Genocide|yours]]. We get back there and we can fix your world! Together. I promise.|Wolverine and [[Deadpool]]|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
Wolverine approached an awakening [[Deadpool]] in a [[Void|barren wasteland]], stabbing him with his fully-grown claws and lifting him up high when questioning where they are. Deadpool giving a witty remark instead of an answer, Wolverine threw him on his knee. Deadpool, stating how his [[Anchor Being Wolverine|world]] is doomed if they don't confront [[Mr. Paradox|Paradox]], insulted Wolverine for his deeds back in his own [[Mutant Genocide|world]] when he said he didn't care. Offended, Wolverine stabbed Deadpool in his back, only for Deadpool to shoot him in both of his sides when he flipped behind him and brought him to the ground. Wolverine thrusted his head back and threw him against the pruned {{WPS|20th Century Fox}} logo.
[[File:Wolverine & Deadpool in the Void.jpg|thumb|{{AltFloat}}|Wolverine prepares to attack [[Sabretooth]]]]
In a standoff, Wolverine prepared his claws before charging at Deadpool while dodging his bullets. Once he was out of them, Deadpool used his [[Deadpool's Katanas|katanas]] and "baby knife" to stab Wolverine, these items being pierced through Wolverine's body. Wolverine was halted from decapitating Deadpool with the promise of having the [[TVA]] fix his world if they cooperate. Their attention was called to a cloaked figure, [[Johnny Storm]], whom alerted them of an approaching team of [[Cassandra Nova's Henchmen|someone's henchmen]]. This included a [[Glossary#Variant|Variant]] of [[Sabretooth]], who challenged Wolverine. Deadpool spruced Wolverine up from the fight they had for the moment people have been waiting decades for. Telling Deadpool to shut up, Wolverine charged towards Sabretooth, beheading him with his claws. Despite their efforts, Wolverine, Deadpool and Storm, who failed to fight [[Pyro]] as the Human Torch, were captured and taken to a [[Cassandra Nova's Compound|compound]]. Wolverine and Deadpool were informed by Storm of the Void's basics; facing [[Alioth]] or working for "[[Cassandra Nova|her]]," and about a [[Resistance]] with a [[Resistance Hideout|hideout]] in the Borderlands.{{Ref|DW}}

====[[Escape from Cassandra Nova's Compound]]====
[[File:The Wolverine.jpg|{{AltFloat}}|Wolverine heads towards his escape]]
{{Quote|If there's a chance [[Resistance|they]] know how to get out of [[Void|here]], we find [[Mr. Paradox|him]] and make those [[Time Variance Authority|TVA fuckers]] fix my shit like you fucking promised."<br>"I smell quest.|Wolverine and [[Deadpool]]|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
Arriving at the [[Cassandra Nova's Compound|compound]], Wolverine and [[Deadpool]] saw a balded figure resembling [[Hub:Charles Xavier|Charles Xavier]] exit [[Giant-Man/Pruned Giant-Man|Giant-Man]]'s skull. Wolverine debunked the person being Xavier, yet not believing that she was [[Professor X/Cassandra Nova Birthed|Xavier]]'s pruned twin [[Cassandra Nova]]. Upon freeing them, Deadpool twisted [[Johnny Storm]]'s words about Nova. With her telepathic powers, Nova skinned Storm alive, Wolverine faulting Deadpool for it. Though Deadpool proceeded to ask for Nova's help, Nova sought for an alliance with Wolverine, given their backstories and pruning. Going on to talk about her Xavier, she asked Wolverine if [[Professor X/Mutant Genocide|his]] also made him feel "safe." Replying that [[mutants]] are never safe, Wolverine attacked Nova and was sunk into the ground. After Nova uncovered Deadpool's memories by phasing her hand through his head, Wolverine stabbed her from behind, though he was simply pushed back. Upon [[Alioth]]'s approach, Wolverine enabled a nearby metal suit's rocket boot to fly away, Deadpool latching onto him.
[[File:Wolverine laughs at Wade.png|thumb|{{AltFloat}}|Logan laughs about [[Wade Wilson|Wilson]]'s toupee]]
Wolverine and Deadpool landed on a cliff, Deadpool forcing his baby knife out of Wolverine's buttocks. Wolverine instigated a rule; only he talks, despite Deadpool doubting the rule. Wolverine planned to get back to [[Paradox]] by finding the [[Resistance]] Storm mentioned earlier, enlist their help with their escape and threaten the [[TVA]] into fixing his [[Mutant Genocide|world]]. Wolverine then spotted a [[Joe's Diner|diner]] from afar, in which he would search for anything with alcohol in it. Sitting by an unmasked Wilson, Logan questioned the few spots of hair on his head. Wilson replied at he wore a toupee that nobody knew of, Logan snickering when assured that everybody knew. Wilson then asked for his backstory before a third act flashback would explain it, Logan telling him to go fuck himself. Wilson talked about how his [[Wolverine/Anchor Being Wolverine|version of the Wolverine]] was regarded as a hero, "''the'' [[X-Men/Anchor Being Wolverine|X-Man]]," only for Logan to say he isn't in his own.
[[File:Wolverine, Dogpool & Wade Wilson.jpg|thumb|{{AltFloat}}|Wolverine and [[Deadpool]] come across [[Dogpool]]]]
Continuing their travels to the Borderlands, Wolverine asked Deadpool what exactly happened to his Wolverine, Deadpool detailing his sacrifice to save his young clone named [[X-23]]. Deadpool went on to tell him that, per [[Blind Al]], pain teaches people who they are, Wolverine only remarking Bilnd Al's name. The two are met by a [[Dogs|dog]] that "[[Nicepool]]," a member of the hostile [[Deadpool Corps]] that ran after the dog, named [[Mary Puppins]], otherwise known as Dogpool. Wolverine asked Nicepool for directions to the Borderlands, Nicepool telling them head towards the west and offering them the ''[[Ol' Betsy]]'' {{WPS|Honda Odyssey}} to travel in.{{Ref|DW}}

====Meeting the Resistance====
[[File:Wolverine at the forest.jpg|thumb|{{AltFloat}}|Wolverine prepares to attack [[Deadpool]]]]
{{Quote|You know what? You're a fucking joke. No wonder the [[Avengers]] didn't take you. Or the [[X-Men/Anchor Being Wolverine|X-Men]], and they'll take fuckin' anyone. I mean, you are a ridiculous, immature, half-wit moron. I have never met a sadder, more attention-starved, jabbering little prick in my ''entire life''. And that says a lot 'cause I've been alive for more than two hundred fucking years. And I'll tell ya, that [[Cassandra Nova|bald chick]]  was right about one thing. You will ''never'' save the world. You couldn't even save a relationship with a goddamn [[Vanessa Carlysle|stripper]]! And motherfucker, I wish I could say you'd die alone, but it's one of God's best jokes that you ''can't'' die! Except that's on all of us!... What? Got nothing to say, Mouth?|Wolverine to [[Deadpool]]|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
On their way to the [[Resistance Hideout]], Wolverine constantly told [[Deadpool]] to quit talking about his [[Wolverine Suit|suit]] and doing the gestures he made. Wolverine is questioned what the first thing he will do "if" his world is fixed, prompting Wolverine to abruptly step on the ''[[Ol' Betsy]]''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s breaks. Coming to the conclusion Deadpool was lying the whole time and that he has no idea if the TVA has the ability to "fix" a world, Wolverine stabs Deadpool in his leg. Deadpool yelped, exclaiming that he made an "educated wish" as he needed Wolverine to save his friends back in [[Earth-10005]]. Wolverine hinged on his mention of an "educated wish," delivering a prolonged and especially insulting speech to upset Deadpool. He left Deadpool speechless until he stated that he will fight him, Wolverine scoffing at the idea. He was however punched in the face. Wolverine punched back, engaging in their duel inside the car.
[[File:Deadpool & Wolverine Trailer (105).png|thumb|{{AltFloat}}|Logan gurgles [[Gambit]]'s liquor]]
The two fought until they both got tired, driven to the Resistance Hideout in their sleep. Deadpool awakened while a drunk Logan chugged down a bottle of beer he found. Upon the introductions of [[Elektra/Forgotten Elektra|Elektra]], [[Blade/Universe Defender Blade|Blade]] and [[Gambit]], Wolverine's bottle, belonging to Gambit, was shattered by the owner's playing card. Wolverine simply threw the broken bottle away in exchange for another. Deadpool asked by whom they were brought to the hideout, leading to [[X-23]]'s introduction, Logan's alternate daughter whom called herself Laura. Deadpool also learned of the [[Resistance]]'s fallen teammates, which included [[Johnny Storm]]. While Deadpool assured them he was still thriving, Logan believed that he'd been in utter pain were he still alive. Nonetheless, Deadpool gets the Resistance on board with fighting for their home universes by making [[Cassandra Nova]] help them escape the [[Void]] by planting [[Juggernaut's Helmet]] onto her head. Logan told them their all goners.
[[File:Deadpool & Wolverine Trailer (64).png|thumb|{{AltFloat}}|Logan tells [[Laura]] his backstory]]
That night, Wolverine sat by a fire outside the hideout and was joined by Laura, whom told him she noticed he shared the same mannerisms as the [[Wolverine/Anchor Being Wolverine|Logan]] she knew. Despite her stating he was a good man, Logan was convinced he wasn't, telling Laura of his many wrongdoings that got many people, such as the [[X-Men/Mutant Genocide|X-Men]] killed. Logan denied to joining the Resistance, heading for [[Cassandra Nova's Compound]] by sun up, and told Laura that they've got the wrong guy. Laura stated that he always was the "wrong guy."{{Ref|DW}}

====[[Attack on Cassandra Nova's Compound|Escaping the Void]]====
[[File:Deadpool & Wolverine Trailer (129).png|thumb|{{AltFloat}}|Wolverine and [[Deadpool]] enter [[Earth-10005]]]]
{{Quote|I know your [[Professor X/Cassandra Nova Birthed|brother]]. As much I wanna fucking kill you, every bone in my body wants to fucking kill you! [[Professor X/Mutant Genocide|He]] would not let me stand here and watch you die. Take [[Deadpool|your]] hands off. This is for him. This is for Charles.|Wolverine to [[Cassandra Nova]]|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
The [[Resistance]] barged through [[Cassandra Nova's Compound]] the next day, Wolverine exiting out of the ''[[Ol' Betsy]]''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s trunk, standing in front of the car alongside the team. Wolverine and [[Deadpool]] fought a couple of [[Cassandra Nova's Henchmen]] before charging towards [[Cassandra Nova]] herself, Nova flicking Deadpool away to face Wolverine. Wolverine tried to attack Nova, but had his claws forced into the floor. Nova then infiltrated Wolverine's mind, meeting Logan walking by the graves of those Logan had killed. Logan told Nova that the cause was his neglect of the [[X-Men/Mutant Genocide|X-Men]]'s distress call, prompting his murderous rampage. He admitted that he only wished to be the man that he was in [[Professor X/Mutant Genocide|Xavier]]'s eyes and freedom, which Nova promised him. Wolverine revealed that he played her, Deadpool putting on [[Juggernaut's Helmet]] on Nova's head. Nova, after revealing that the helmet limited her powers, was shot by [[Pyro]], whom Wolverine punched unconscious. Wolverine urged Deadpool to take the helmet off before she died, for Xavier's sake. Upon removing it himself, Nova used a [[Doctor Strange/Pruned Doctor Strange|Doctor Strange]] [[Glossary#Variant|Variant]]'s [[Sling Ring]] to open an [[Inter-Dimensional Portal]] to [[Earth-10005]], Wolverine and Deadpool leaping through before [[Alioth]] came again.
[[File:Deadpool & Wolverine Everyone (18).png|thumb|{{AltFloat}}|Wolverine and [[Deadpool]] land on a {{WPS|Kia Carnival}}]]
Wolverine and Deadpool crash-landed upon the {{WPS|Kia Carnival}} Deadpool's friend [[Peter Wisdom]] was selling to the Chipman family at [[Drive Max]]. One of the children recognized Wolverine, Deadpool joking that [[Walt Disney Studios]] is going to have [[Hugh Jackman]] portraying him till he becomes 90 years old. Wolverine and Deadpool subsequently left.{{Ref|DW}}

====Fighting the Deadpool Corps====
[[File:Deadpool questions Paradox.png|thumb|{{AltFloat}}|Wolverine and [[Deadpool]] confront [[Mr. Paradox]]]]
{{Quote|Are you ready?"<br>"I get to kill a [[Deadpool Corps|hundred yous]]? Fuck, yeah, I'm ready. [[Dogpool|You]] don't wanna see this, bub.|[[Deadpool]] and Wolverine|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
Wolverine and [[Deadpool]] confronted [[Paradox]] at the entrance to the subway where he was guarding the [[Time Ripper]], only for a [[Inter-Dimensional Portal|second portal]] to open behind them, with [[Pyro]] emerging from it and trying to warn Paradox before being killed by [[Cassandra Nova|Nova]]. Nova then delved into Paradox's mind, discovered the Time Ripper and decided to use it for her own gain. Logan and Wade confronted Paradox at the entrance to the subway where he was guarding the Time Ripper, only for a second portal to open behind them, with Pyro emerging and trying to warn Paradox before being killed by Nova. Nova then delved into Paradox's mind and discovered the Time Ripper and decided to use it for his own gain, before telekinetically pushing the two mutants back into a [[Liefeld's|foot cream establishment]].
[[File:Wolverine and Dogpool.jpg|thumb|{{AltFloat}}|Wolverine shields himself with [[Dogpool]]]]
Upon recovering, the duo saw [[Dogpool]] and [[Nicepool]] exit the portal, but Logan subsequently smelled a large number of Deadpool's scents also coming from the [[Void]]. As the [[Deadpool Corps]] came to the streets in full force, Wade forced Wolverine to hold Dogpool while he tried to reason his other variants working for Nova. The alternate [[Hub:Wade Wilson|Deadpools]] didn't listen to reason and started shooting in the crowd. Hiding behind a car to escape the bullets, Wolverine accused Deadpool of having used Nicepool as a human shield, the latter proving to be devoid of healing factor. Deadpool tried to reach a donut stand under the pretext that there were surgical kits, but Wolverine had already understood that Deadpool just wanted to use Nicepool as a human shield again. Following Nicepool's head exploding, Wolverine used Dogpool to dissuade the Deadpools from shooting him while he joined his Deadpool behind the stand. The duo briefly rant about Nicepool's fate, with Deadpool taking the opportunity to retrieve his golden guns, then asked Wolverine if he was ready to fight, to which Wolverine responded that he was totally ready to kill hundreds of Deadpool [[Glossary#V|Variants]].
[[File:Big Slow Motion Action Sequence.jpg|thumb|{{AltFloat}}|Wolverine and [[Deadpool]] face the [[Deadpool Corps]]]]
Facing the Deadpool Corps, Wolverine put on his hidden mask, much to the astonishment of Deadpool who thought that he kept the mask for special occasions, and Wolverine replied that he mainly puts it on to kill. Gun and claws out, Wolverine and Deadpool rushed at the variants and quickly massacred most of them in a bloody manner while taking wounds themselves that did not stop them. They are briefly pushed back but quickly regain their initial upper hand and eliminate the last Deadpools inside a bus, before practically exiting through the rear window, Wolverine landing but Deadpool missing on his side. As soon as they noticed [[Babypool]] laughing at them, they watched their victim regenerate afterwards, then were surrounded by them. Suddenly, [[Peter Wisdom]] joined the scene, the Deadpool Corps having recognized him since they also had a Peter in their universe, completely diverted their attention to him, so Wolverine and Deadpool took advantage of the inattention to enter the subway.{{Ref|DW}}

====Saving All Timelines====
{{Quote|You got a whole world to get back to. I got nothing. Give me this."<br>"Hey. I waited a long time for this team-up. Y'know something? You're the ''best'' [[Hub:Logan|Wolverine]]."<br>"...Say hi for your friends to me.|Wolverine and [[Deadpool]]|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
Entering the subway station, Wolverine and [[Deadpool]] met [[Paradox]], distressed over [[Cassandra Nova]]'s plan to destroy all universes except the [[Void]]. Wolverine asked him how to shut the [[Time Ripper]] down, forcing Paradox onto the control panel when he said he didn't know. Deadpool remarked on the intimidation his mask exuded, comparing it to {{WPS|Batman}}'s. Paradox explained that the Time Ripper was fed by matter and anti-matter feeds, and Nova was redirecting the Time Ripper's power to exterminate every timeline. The only way to destroy the Time Ripper was to create a circuit between the two feeds, although whoever created the circuit would be atomized, despite the duo's regenerative healing factors.

Approaching the feeds' chamber below, Wolverine halted Deadpool to repeat Paradox's words on the inevitability of a sacrifice. Deadpool decided that he would be the circuit because he brought Wolverine into the mess and lied to his face. Wolverine echoed Deadpool's mention of an "educated wish," stating that it must be him, seeing as Deadpool had a world to get back to while he did not. Wolverine opened the chamber's door but was pushed outside by Deadpool, who sacrificed himself instead. With one feed in hand, Deadpool reached for the other as Wolverine tried to barge through the door. With time running out and Deadpool not being able to reach the second feed, Wolverine managed to break through the door and grab the second feed in his claws, grabbing Deadpool's hand with his and effectively creating the circuit. The energy from the feeds caused the part of his [[Wolverine Suit|suit]] that covered his upper body to explode, exposing his abs. Wolverine reminisced about his past and the person he had become as he screamed until the Time Ripper exploded.

When [[Paradox]]'s boss, [[Hunter B-15]], appeared on the scene, he tried to make it seem like he did nothing wrong and that Wolverine and Deadpool had sacrificed themselves, but his lie was revealed when the duo exited the chamber unharmed. Logan handed his mask to [[Ralph]], who stared blindingly at his pecs, which Deadpool covered up with a [[TVA]] jacket. Deadpool explained that they survived thanks to the power of a Deadpool and a Wolverine listening to {{WPS|Madonna}}'s "{{WPS|Like a Prayer}}". Despite the reckless actions of Deadpool, bringing an Omega-level [[Mutants|mutant]] into his timeline, B-15 showed Logan and Deadpool that the [[Earth-10005]] timeline was growing back, advising them to rest before they'd be called. Deadpool joked that Logan would be portrayed by [[Hugh Jackman]] until the latter turned 90. Besides asking for the [[Resistance]] to be returned to their home universes, Deadpool also requested for Logan's actions back in his world to be undone. However, B-15 declined the latter request, as Logan became a better man due to his experiences in his [[Mutant Genocide|universe]].{{Ref|DW}}

